# A RESOLVE LINE FROM ANOTHER STATE OF THE FILE. The id is the one this fixture's plan renders; the digest
# is the well-formed sha256 the file carried BEFORE the note now at its foot was appended — a real digest
# of a real earlier state, not a made-up string. So the refusal can only be the staleness law: an id whose
# bytes have moved is not a licence to rewrite whichever occurrence now happens to sit at that extent,
# which is the failure the digest is here for, because the id alone is positional and an edit above the
# occurrence moves every id below it.
resolve fixtures/reference_migration_refused/dag/gunbc/reference_migration_unresolved_citer.dag@437-446 ee3e8423c4a5c8446607bea804479ac1d6dd20308b276a348e5bca758af46a26 => gunbc.reference_migration_unresolved_citer::reference_migration_unresolved_citer_value
